Brief info about Vinted&nbsp;

Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we're looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life - or even a third.
The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:

Vinted Marketplace is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.

Vinted Go enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.

Vinted Pay is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.

Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania's first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we've grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&nbsp;

Information about the position&nbsp;

Vinted is building out its compliance function for the EU Digital Services Act (DSA) and equivalent online safety regimes, including the UK Online Safety Act. These regimes run on a fixed calendar of public deliverables: transparency reports every six months, an annual systemic risk assessment, an annual independent audit, and a continuous feed of content moderation decisions to the Commission’s DSA Transparency Database.

In this position, you’ll&nbsp;

• Own the production calendar for every recurring public report under the DSA (Articles 15, 24 and 42) and equivalent regimes, and land each one on its statutory deadline;

• Gather and reconcile the reported data with Content Moderation, Customer Support, Product and Data - moderation volumes and outcomes, notice-and-action and complaint figures, moderation headcount and language coverage, monthly active recipients per Member State - and produce the first complete draft of each report in the Commission’s harmonised templates (Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2835);

• Interrogate the numbers before anyone outside sees them: reconcile to source, explain movements between periods, challenge the owning team where a figure does not hold up;

• Run the annual independent audit day to day as point of contact for the auditor appointed under Article 37 - information requests, walkthroughs, evidence packs, factual accuracy reviews - under the direction of the Head of the Compliance Function;

• Convert audit findings into a tracked remediation plan, chase it to closure, and produce the audit implementation report under Article 37(6) and the public package under Article 42(4);

• Build and maintain the obligation register and control library - each duty mapped to its owner, its control and its evidence - and run periodic control testing with Risk Management and Internal Audit &amp; Control;

• Run the operational side of the annual risk assessment under Articles 34 and 35 and draft responses to requests for information from the Commission, the Digital Services Coordinator and other regulators.

About you&nbsp;

• At least 4 years in regulatory compliance, audit, regulatory reporting or GRC, where you personally produced deliverables that went to a regulator or an external auditor;

• Working knowledge of the DSA, in particular Articles 15, 24, 34-37, 41 and 42; UK Online Safety Act or comparable regimes a strong plus;

• You do not need to be a qualified lawyer - a legal qualification is welcome but not required;

• Demonstrated owner

REQUISITOS MANDATÓRIOS

• Conhecimento em Segurança do Trabalho, SGSMS e SGI, preferencialmente no segmento de Exploração e Produção de Óleo e Gás, com familiaridade com processos industriais contínuos e atividades similares às desenvolvidas nos locais objeto deste contrato;

• Conhecimento em atividades em plantas industriais; Participação em simulados de emergências de grande amplitude em plantas industriais; Formação específica ou experiência prática para realização de avaliações de HO;

• Leitura e interpretação de desenhos e normas técnicas, e interpretação de fluxogramas de processo;

• Manuseio de sistemas informatizados de gestão de segurança do trabalho;

• Conhecimentos de leitura em inglês básico;

• Conhecimento dos softwares do pacote Office;

• Conhecimento da legislação em gestão de segurança do trabalho aplicável ao setor de petróleo e gás;

• Capacidade de trabalho em equipe;

• Conhecimentos de simulados de emergências de grande amplitude em plantas industriais e avaliações de HO.

• Conhecimento em projetos e outros.

&nbsp;

ESCOLARIDADE&nbsp;

Curso Técnico em Segurança do Trabalho, com registro profissional ativo no Ministério do Trabalho e Emprego (MTE).

&nbsp;

REQUISITOS DESEJÁVEIS

• Curso de especialização com carga horária mínima de 40 horas em Auditor Interno ou Externo ISO 14001, 45001, 9001, Auditor SGI, Licenciamento Ambiental, Gerenciamento de Resíduos e/ou outros correlatos.

&nbsp;

ATRIBUIÇÕES

• O profissional deste cargo atuará com a Gestão Administrativa e Operacional das atividades de SMS, perfazendo indicadores, avaliações de riscos e auditorias ambientais, monitoramentos, elaboração de relatórios e documentações técnicas para apresentação junto a órgãos competentes.&nbsp;

• Orientar e coordenar o sistema de segurança do trabalho, investigando riscos e causas de acidentes, analisando esquemas de prevenção.

• Inspecionar locais, instalações e equipamentos da empresa e determinar fatores de riscos de acidentes. Inspecionar os postos de combate a incêndios, examinando as mangueiras, hidrantes, extintores e equipamentos de proteção contra incêndios.

• Apoiar a investigação incidentes, examinando as condições da ocorrência, para identificar suas causas e propor as providências cabíveis.

• Treinar os funcionários da empresa sobre normas de segurança, combate à incêndios e demais medidas de prevenção de acidentes.

• Participar de reuniões sobre segurança no trabalho.

